        "flipMissedHeading": "Nothing to replay this time",
        "flipLandedNoTells": "It read as an ordinary brief with nothing to catch this time. Next you sit with the assistant for real work and handle what comes at you.",
        "defendIntro": "Go through the messages and decide what to do with each one. You can't reliably spot a fake voice or face, so when a message asks for money, data or a sign-in, check another way, on a number or channel you already hold. Work through them at your own pace.",
        "noBlameLine": "The demo fools nearly everyone, and it was built to; the assistant is useful and most of what it writes is right. A miss just shows where to check next time.",
        "mondayCard": "On Monday: before you paste into the assistant, take out what the task doesn't need and never paste a password; before you send what it writes, check the figures and the claims against the source; and if a call, video or email pushes you to move money, send data or sign in, stop and check another way, using the route in the box below.",
        "defendOnly": "These messages were built to look right, a real supplier's address, a voice you know, a face you trust. Any you were caught out by are shown below, with what gave each one away and why checking another way works whoever is speaking.",
